<node id="&quot;INTEREST&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INTEREST RATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest is the cost associated with borrowing funds, specified for both Lenders and Borrower based on their respective types of loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The amount charged to the Borrower on the refunded taxes calculated from the date such refund is paid over, related to refund processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cost charged by the Lender on the loans provided to the Borrower, typically expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cost incurred by the borrower for the use of borrowed funds, expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cost incurred or additional amounts due as a result of unpaid taxes or liabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cost of borrowing that the Borrower is obligated to pay, as specified in the agreement."</data>
