<node id="&quot;FEDERAL FUNDS RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A fluctuating rate per annum that is part of the definition for the Alternate Base Rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A key interest rate determined by U.S. banks for overnight borrowing, used as a reference point for various financial transactions, including loan pricing."&lt;SEP&gt;"An important economic indicator proportionate to short-term interest rates for overnight lending between banks, which influences broader financial rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reference interest rate used for calculating any payment due to the Issuing Lender after the payment due date."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reference interest rate used for compensation on erroneous payments under the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"the average rate charged to Citibank on such day on such transactions as determined by the Administrative Agent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbdb56df8c98cd2c1ef5d8cac7dcfbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77861f28d368fffce8cb139bd90225db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-303d4111dcc6924456507f281b537f2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2312b6c1d8ad4b95ad6661f4fa1b286f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe12461084bb91bf3fa92e79fc2890e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b1eebe2d58609217c8bdecde0f604c</data>
