<node id="&quot;REGULATION U&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulation U defines margin stock and establishes rules regarding the use of margin stock as collateral by lenders and borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regulation U is a Federal Reserve Regulation that restricts the use of credit in connection with the purchase of securities and must be adhered to by the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regulation U is mentioned to clarify the Borrower's restrictions on extending credit related to margin stock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Regulation U means Regulation U of the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System as from time to time in effect and any successor or other regulation or official interpretation of said Board of Governors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9a78ac18a08e4ac60633a82d5e95b9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f0c9708e0c2a6fd25d8fab0cb14da5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f7f879e70c1c09e23862d87cf18c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a5395386d972c6903e35205b0eb8cb</data>
