<node id="&quot;AUTHORIZED OFFICER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"OBLIGOR"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Authorized Officer is an individual who has the authority to certify and sign documents on behalf of the Borrower, particularly concerning compliance with the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Authorized Officer of the Borrower certifies that specified conditions are met before the Extension Date."&lt;SEP&gt;"An appointed representative of the borrower who is authorized to make requests and execute transactions under the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to officers like the President, Chairman, CEO, CFO, etc., of the Borrower who have the authority to act on behalf of the Borrower regarding notices or agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Signatory responsible for certifying satisfaction of requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"The designated individual responsible for signing the Borrowing Notice and ensuring compliance with loan agreements."</data>
