<node id="&quot;ERISA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defined in terms of the legal obligations under the Employee Retirement Income Security Act."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which governs employee benefit plans in the United States, including standards for plans and fiduciaries."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which includes provisions impacting how Lender obligations are structured under benefit plans."&lt;SEP&gt;"ERISA refers to the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, which the Borrower must comply with as part of their legal obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, as amended, including rules or regulations promulgated thereunder."&lt;SEP&gt;"the act governing employee benefits, mentioned in the context of Foreign Pension Plans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98873f0978b82c2fd29714e88f71122d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f0b98aec52fb64b5625c54126b83ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6eb63f465378ef1651901525bcc3ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84f13ebb93a2379c4e024700e6b9a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe12461084bb91bf3fa92e79fc2890e</data>
