  <data key="d1">"A loan type that is denominated in a currency other than that of the borrower, affecting interest rates and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another type of loan option provided under the agreement that may be selected by the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Another type of loan that is part of the Advances that can be selected by the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eurocurrency Loans refer to loans that are issued in foreign currencies and require specific consents from lenders and the Administrative Agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eurocurrency Loans refer to loans that are made in a currency not native to the country in which the loan is being made, involved in international lending practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans that are issued in currencies other than Dollars, convertible into Dollars in the London interbank market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obligation of such Lender to make or continue Eurocurrency Loans or to convert Alternate Base Rate Loans to Eurocurrency Loans shall be suspended."&lt;SEP&gt;"if any Lender determines that any law has made it unlawful, or that any Governmental Authority has asserted..."</data>
