  <data key="d1">"Refers to the amount equal to the value of a draft when converted into dollars, important for establishing payment obligations in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Dollar Equivalent is the conversion of foreign currency amounts into U.S. dollars for reimbursement purposes, as determined by the rules outlined in the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The converted amount reflecting the value of foreign currencies in terms of the Dollar, critical for financial calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The equivalent amount in Dollars determined by the Administrative Agent for amounts denominated in Foreign Currency or Additional L/C Currency."&lt;SEP&gt;"The equivalent amount of a draft paid under a Letter of Credit denominated in a Foreign Currency, calculated in U.S. dollars."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a8f315e0d4cc8cd2accfbbe5da06a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f248cd4e812b91a37d2ecd4ea05ab17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb0e9645dbfb8d0a148e453d64143d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdb56df8c98cd2c1ef5d8cac7dcfbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505094570d348d1eb98341b07550afb9</data>
