<node id="&quot;FACILITY TERMINATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATURITY DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Facility Termination Date" refers to a critical and definitive date marking the conclusion of a specified financial facility or loan arrangement. This date is significant for all parties involved, as it defines when the Borrower must fulfill all outstanding obligations, including repaying any outstanding loans and other unpaid obligations in full. 

The Facility Termination Date indicates the endpoint of the available funding under the facility agreement and also signifies when the Commitments to lend expire automatically. Notably, it is the final date by which all financial agreements related to the facility, including those concerning the issuance or renewal of Letters of Credit, must be concluded.

In terms of operational specifics, no Interest Period may extend beyond this date, and it represents the earliest relevant date for the conclusion of the agreement, which may be influenced by various operational conditions and business day considerations. Overall, the Facility Termination Date serves as the definitive moment when all related agreements and obligations cease to be effective.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb0e9645dbfb8d0a148e453d64143d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18692c17359acf3a4cc5b222ca8d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d48c01f13ec86692718a0f2e1aa00e7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f4a3c6e75cb695a5901b1f0b84cdb53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0d8174003f4772facdd639b135093a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e914eec878b034344a2461c17601e972&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf07809d1746fad0fc15e800a6e13c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45eacffe710b8a1539c2b0e28ec9c0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eb96d7191b0699d9084c61a58e1f937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16bc6fb03d3fef88e01a6cce943dfcd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626e172089dfc80733dbdc3d5a655994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b24f224a12be42ba1f1dbc4b72037c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81c89a4f0646075ebbb8d120c81f1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94c0222f445089aa6e963934b40deca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fa9414c8f55fa15b04b2759525b64c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40b4e9dc14bb67b22b82308d7b947&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b1eebe2d58609217c8bdecde0f604c</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EFFECTIVE DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EXECUTED DATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Effective Date" refers to a specific date on which certain conditions must be satisfied and confirmed, marking the commencement of obligations and responsibilities under an agreement. It signifies the date when the agreement officially takes effect, leading to the obligations becoming enforceable and legally binding between the parties involved. It is crucial for determining when particular agreements, including financial disclosures and the issuance of Letters of Credit, come into force. 

For the agreement to become effective, all stipulated conditions must be met, including those specified in Section 4.01. This date is also significant for the Borrower, as it is the point after which subsidiaries may guarantee obligations under Loan Documents. Furthermore, the Effective Date is referenced in determining commitments of Lenders and marks the start of obligations as indicated in the Commitment Schedule.

In summary, the Effective Date is the essential date signifying the beginning of enforceable obligations and the commencement of the terms dictated by the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1183a800fd6a9854db176c7afeee466f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3e5cabd1adf8bfb109a8c35cc714a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128157f36e29f84a8759014f2c0bac7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94c0222f445089aa6e963934b40deca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3233fa8d7d4c0809069a1ba9245215cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4775969ba9c4358815c44ba19ab6cf61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3c1b09c7a3b24aa925d3f14133dc8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6650c2933728727b65a678ab18928dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5cae935d5ac1c45cef47e54948aebca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51e0b942fc38bb2172bde4cb6d8e8480&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2784e996404efd1f12a712b7977889c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4624e829973bed7d3dbe1f2bc639fd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f7f879e70c1c09e23862d87cf18c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d92f3ae85f5d9dc7cd636aa2549b31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e55ec0667ebf49101d269a842009d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57790ed9c8601659e5a900ae22c9e87f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23cc38126f5fc772e7c16a84edaa089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc596f8efd3d960e41a0c7ead13fb1fe</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ISSUING LENDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Issuing Lenders" are a specific category of financial institutions that play a crucial role in the context of loan agreements, particularly in relation to issuing letters of credit. They are responsible for providing various forms of financial support which includes extending loans and guaranteeing obligations under the terms of the agreement. Issuing Lenders are entitled to make claims in judicial proceedings and are involved in enforcing certain loan documents. 

In carrying out their functions, they incur expenses related to enforcing or protecting their rights under the agreement and have responsibilities that include consent to certain assignments. They also face exposure linked to defaulting lenders, which can impact their obligations and financial standing. Furthermore, Issuing Lenders participate in the loan approval process and collaborate with other lenders to ensure the efficient management of the loan arrangement.

Overall, the Issuing Lenders are integral to the provision of letters of credit and other temporary financing arrangements, facilitating smooth transactions for the Borrower while adhering to the stipulations outlined within the broader financing agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c340d96c262ce6b46bd104eff6e1e898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e198d77431c861292a99379d78c97060&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-175c18fb247e3700a956581f912d57df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca92fb46e43aac35741ad94be06baf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08590c6f860ab659cec13d7e2426aa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443cceb6eea0f4b1688789c95181be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-367efea91f14c308908cbf46f7b778de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ba5dd3dff3a1a68f89de13b8aa21f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4438bf9135054e1ff77226fc332e8268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbd5056a9b1d822dcccb189f309820c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0d8174003f4772facdd639b135093a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9653286dcc9ab1fd5889964b3252c74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2b28c1dc4239fb1b4dc694b26a9338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a78ac18a08e4ac60633a82d5e95b9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef03c2a3bc83b467c592d30c98456018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-904c0cc387dffe2b87a7d3f92f2a414f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebd046b77e404961bb2e85f280bf3765</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SCHEDULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"BUSINESS DAY" is defined as a standard operational day recognized for normal banking procedures, during which financial institutions are open for business, excluding weekends and federal holidays. This definition is crucial for various aspects of agreements, including the timing of notices, communications, repayments, loan funding, and the calculation of interest periods. Specifically, a Business Day pertains to any day when banks conduct typical financial operations, which directly influences deadlines for transactions, cash collateralization, issuance of Letters of Credit, and the determination of interest, such as the Secured Overnight Financing Rate (SOFR).

In contractual contexts, a Business Day impacts the processing of payments and notifications, the execution of loan transactions, and the validity of communications. It is also relevant for determining the timeline for obligations under the agreement and for actions that need to occur within specified periods. The last Business Day of each calendar month holds particular importance for financial reporting and planning. Overall, the concept of a Business Day serves as a foundation for various critical financial operations and obligations outlined in contractual agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-eb2d822d34cd4895bb4832559ec6c10d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca04737f45a17e3fb227522494264c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a575e820a47b3c2dbd1089d67ed6dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d277b1d67ae447d64c60885603bfc58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a248a4d561291c597b0a80f7d7b6b35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ea2c276659bea1c507ce8061fac280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88c08aa03f546119db2aa5503fb5d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ff3410f6697f7d5609929e33fcaa0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3233fa8d7d4c0809069a1ba9245215cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6e2d4916072445b0d7943e6df0abe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c87b9e7043c61cd132d4af9cb79a608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdb56df8c98cd2c1ef5d8cac7dcfbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f4a3c6e75cb695a5901b1f0b84cdb53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b237e569bb47a68fc1dfc5a53add55c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4792b5b0b77bf53c196055d4d402e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f248cd4e812b91a37d2ecd4ea05ab17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07fc883538bb5884b759a6d95b627c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b2d3addc3724118fcaa9cbe2d864f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b1eebe2d58609217c8bdecde0f604c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e55ec0667ebf49101d269a842009d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f007ed84b09aaafd346209ff90f4b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da412b37f50503895e084a2932cc427</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETTERS OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LETTER OF CREDIT"</data>
  <data key="d1">Letters of Credit are financial instruments that serve as guarantees issued by banks, specifically by Issuing Lenders, to ensure payment to beneficiaries under specified conditions. These instruments are designed to secure payment obligations of borrowers, allowing them access to funds in relation to commitment details outlined in credit agreements. The guarantees provided by Letters of Credit ensure that payments will be made, contingent upon pre-defined terms and conditions. 

The guarantees may involve aspects such as collateral and are critical in ordinary business transactions that require reimbursement obligations. In particular, Letters of Credit are issued for the account of the borrower and allow for transactions in foreign currencies, ensuring a smooth and reliable financial exchange. They provide essential assurance to lenders and facilitate financial transactions related to borrowed money obligations.

Specifically, institutions like CITIBANK, N.A. issue these guarantees on behalf of borrowers to honor financial commitments. The guarantees can also be subject to the consent of the Issuing Lender and the Administrative Agent, further defining the intricacies involved in these agreements. Overall, Letters of Credit represent a vital tool in financial arrangements, ensuring that beneficiaries receive payment as stipulated within the associated contracts.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c340d96c262ce6b46bd104eff6e1e898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec8822f0ae2be723af299c5930b2ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07d22735da3f44da96c1e4f1bea670b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08590c6f860ab659cec13d7e2426aa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6eb63f465378ef1651901525bcc3ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bfa88e74387e9ded8d6d400ce29b863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-367efea91f14c308908cbf46f7b778de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bddd2264c99015efb820b7c4e86acbf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9cd184601902e993589a5485493e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c14c7925e4a607de0382cb8d2225da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52bf93d3e20b62a0cd832df66353f563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c120a778327f296345bae50f8d1508f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2b28c1dc4239fb1b4dc694b26a9338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c088153227b34dfaa95e623edf217ee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18692c17359acf3a4cc5b222ca8d5302&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a73a441bb280da7c7eac26f41db97d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da627f496ed5b278745386e332bef7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6e59cb00ab074fd4164fff2fb0f72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd6d2a03e6e0fe0536790ef81febaf9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0acdd477847e0ceb3f6060dfa6826b3</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;L/C OBLIGATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">L/C Obligations refer to the financial responsibilities and liabilities associated with letters of credit, primarily involving the Borrower's commitments to repay amounts guaranteed by these credits. These obligations arise when letters of credit are issued on behalf of the Borrower, necessitating various financial responsibilities that must be fulfilled under the agreement with multiple lenders.

Specifically, L/C Obligations require the Borrower to secure cash collateral, especially in events affecting the letters of credit, and must not exceed the stipulated L/C Sublimit or violate other specified conditions. The total amount due related to these obligations includes both drawn and undrawn amounts associated with the letters of credit.

The lenders also have responsibilities under the L/C Obligations, which include honoring the letters of credit issued for the Borrower's transactions and the obligation to purchase participations in these obligations as defined in their agreement. Additionally, L/C Obligations encompass the various commitments of the lenders in trade financing contexts and their roles in the assurance of payment provided through letters of credit issued by the Issuing Lender. Thus, they represent a critical component of the financial landscape in transactions involving the Borrower and the lenders.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a8f315e0d4cc8cd2accfbbe5da06a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044c8c17addf705b3a705cce6b061dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca04737f45a17e3fb227522494264c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b2d3addc3724118fcaa9cbe2d864f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443cceb6eea0f4b1688789c95181be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e198d77431c861292a99379d78c97060&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef03c2a3bc83b467c592d30c98456018&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3e5cabd1adf8bfb109a8c35cc714a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-128157f36e29f84a8759014f2c0bac7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c120a778327f296345bae50f8d1508f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6650c2933728727b65a678ab18928dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f8540eaf8f40e45748d1788b0ef6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e7677f7f7b78ac8baeaf00df9e5e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bfb84ae77fdaa5e8c3a97e04c2e26f6</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUSINESS DAYS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SCHEDULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Business Days" refers to a defined period in financial agreements that specifies the days on which certain actions, transactions, and obligations must occur. Business Days are typically operational days during which financial institutions are open, excluding weekends and public holidays. This definition encompasses various aspects such as the issuance of Letters of Credit and the processing of applications, which must happen within these specified days.

In particular, "Business Days" are important for responding to requests for advances or letters of credit, indicating that requests need to be made and responses received within these operational days. For example, the Borrower must provide at least three (3) Business Days’ prior notice to the Administrative Agent for certain actions, and the agreements often stipulate that any due amounts must be settled no later than ten Business Days following a written demand. Moreover, any notes requested by the Borrower must be submitted in writing at least five (5) Business Days before the Closing Date.

Overall, the concept of Business Days establishes a framework for when financial obligations—such as payments, notifications, and transactions—must be executed, ensuring that both parties adhere to the timeliness required for effective operations within the framework of the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7d9cd184601902e993589a5485493e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed9d7d04f3944a560b6db90e5050458&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2784e996404efd1f12a712b7977889c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec8822f0ae2be723af299c5930b2ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d35133a09e796f51c620fe44c317a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da627f496ed5b278745386e332bef7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8779071286711185e7ec64cc9f3e085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23cc38126f5fc772e7c16a84edaa089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d2f0619713166fc84a2c2b0e0230d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-509c304656080c8e86ce3cd455d89065&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6e59cb00ab074fd4164fff2fb0f72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c546287864ea4d788574dbe3580df8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81c89a4f0646075ebbb8d120c81f1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5cae935d5ac1c45cef47e54948aebca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc596f8efd3d960e41a0c7ead13fb1fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b237e569bb47a68fc1dfc5a53add55c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9d82c1146b4efba6097c4e3cc70a41e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2312b6c1d8ad4b95ad6661f4fa1b286f</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "SUBSIDIARIES" refers to companies that are owned or controlled by the Borrower. These entities are integral to the Borrower's overall financial structure and are similarly prohibited from receiving assignments under certain conditions. They are considered in various financial calculations, including earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortization (EBITDA), and are required to provide consolidated financial information alongside the Borrower. 

Moreover, these subsidiaries contribute to the Borrower's financial standing and liabilities, and may have separate financial reporting obligations. They are also expected to utilize acquisition debt in their normal operations and are subject to compliance with the legal and regulatory requirements outlined in relevant agreements. Subsidiaries may be impacted by obligations regarding asset disposition and are associated with environmental liabilities discussed in legal contexts.

The Borrower has the capacity to acquire all or substantially all assets from its subsidiaries under specified conditions. The creditworthiness of these subsidiaries may be evaluated by lenders, highlighting their relevance in the financial operations of the Borrower. Additionally, neither the Borrower nor its subsidiaries or affiliates can participate in the sale of participations, reinforcing their distinct role within the corporate hierarchy. Overall, these subsidiaries play a crucial role in the Borrower's operational and financial landscape.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a5395386d972c6903e35205b0eb8cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb0e9645dbfb8d0a148e453d64143d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1183a800fd6a9854db176c7afeee466f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f007ed84b09aaafd346209ff90f4b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4624e829973bed7d3dbe1f2bc639fd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08590c6f860ab659cec13d7e2426aa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca785d11c173b114c75a86d24a9c1982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1aa9c35788b69a204e6324308aa3b79f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85242d66571c09fe35aa36fa705e26f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f7f879e70c1c09e23862d87cf18c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcfdf8a71bd320a62004e0e384e11c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4ac05f6ad1913c40d66d2f014a76efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455f5d24af85e0e01ce99360a0fe0f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f8540eaf8f40e45748d1788b0ef6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6486173d4e89e0b5a1e51ec7b8969261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7db23745e08dce95f931014f491b519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0acdd477847e0ceb3f6060dfa6826b3</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REQUIRED LENDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "REQUIRED LENDERS" refer to a specified group of lenders that are crucial for making decisions and approvals related to a loan agreement. This group is essential in various contexts, including consenting to amendments, waivers, and other significant changes to the loan terms. 

Required Lenders must agree on critical actions such as objecting to Early Opt-in Elections, the appointment or removal of a successor Administrative Agent, and extending loan terms. Specifically, they hold greater than fifty percent of the Aggregate Commitment on a designated date, and their agreement is necessary to validate extension decisions and consent for modifications related to Indebtedness for Borrowed Money.

Their consent is also mandatory for approving the Benchmark Replacement and for conversions of Dollar-denominated Advances into Eurocurrency Advances. Additionally, Required Lenders play a pivotal role in waiving defaults and agreeing to any changes affecting the terms and conditions of the agreement. They must express satisfaction with specified conditions before the Administrative Agent can proceed with actions under the loan agreement.

Overall, Required Lenders represent the lenders whose collective consent and decision-making authority are vital for operational and financial aspects of the loan, ensuring that all significant adjustments and actions are authorized following the stipulated guidelines in the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d35133a09e796f51c620fe44c317a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d610724a0ad4c9bf19e1e6f7531d7eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dde35fec0c8bee31e9959cd10aeb752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf07809d1746fad0fc15e800a6e13c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f946a950865efa69f83d6930d5a5ebef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3501bf74ffa65326e0d3555b82f8a65d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8682b6b632c76068654dbc45fa760d28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a3e836c8b1039ab574b4d21c75c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660ba35b7b2352a6dcf5d1814a86b611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78df53bf404a8c04f30aed8e096f054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fa9414c8f55fa15b04b2759525b64c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbd5056a9b1d822dcccb189f309820c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7c6cce4fccfd6907fab04622874d2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c120a778327f296345bae50f8d1508f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf894b623f9cbade8155fbff04b0edc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-349e138a26328314f6d91c26c4b4d6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13482f9d41736bece8f6cc18418a9fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9cd9748d004c4b865b0c54ca99b6c09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da412b37f50503895e084a2932cc427</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNMATURED DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Unmatured Default" refers to a condition involving existing defaults that have not yet matured or become actionable under a specific agreement. It describes a scenario where the Borrower has not yet failed to fulfill its obligations, yet there are potential future defaults that could arise based on compliance assessments. This term indicates an event that would constitute a default but is currently not actionable due to the lapse of time or the requirement of notice.

In essence, an Unmatured Default highlights risks that may lead to a default in the future if certain conditions are not met. This situation necessitates that the Borrower ensure compliance with all measures to avoid approaching a default state. It is critical for the Borrower to be aware of the implications of Unmatured Default, as failing to do so could jeopardize their standing under the agreement, especially regarding requests for credit extensions. Importantly, the existence of Unmatured Default does not imply that a default has occurred; rather, it indicates that the Borrower remains at risk unless corrective actions are taken. The concept also emphasizes that, to date, no Unmatured Default has occurred or is continuing, provided the Borrower adheres to the compliance requirements set forth in the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b5a5395386d972c6903e35205b0eb8cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a575e820a47b3c2dbd1089d67ed6dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da627f496ed5b278745386e332bef7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99e694a36ce9e20cd42f9c5918c7a197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fe64f66c3bae5bd7a455b76b08b5bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f0b98aec52fb64b5625c54126b83ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3679e0426d9ba539d7a46289e2bab63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16bc6fb03d3fef88e01a6cce943dfcd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c546287864ea4d788574dbe3580df8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d1e82013d8397017bf069a08e734a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5cae935d5ac1c45cef47e54948aebca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b5bfafb78d3fba9840d96ce7e8fc410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c42000811c18c4fe1fb14e6839c213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7db23745e08dce95f931014f491b519</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "LOAN DOCUMENT" refers to a comprehensive set of legal contracts and agreements that govern the financial relationships between Borrowers and Lenders, detailing the terms and conditions associated with borrowed funds. This term encompasses all documentation related to loan transactions, including specific agreements that outline the rights and obligations of the parties involved, such as the Administrative Agent and Lenders. 

A Loan Document includes critical elements such as payment obligations, tax withholdings, indemnities, and any guarantees that may be involved. These documents serve as an official record of the loan terms, stipulating the responsibilities and potential liabilities of the Borrower and Lenders. Each Loan Document is integral to the contractual framework that shapes the lending and borrowing relationship, providing clarity on the agreements and covenants that must be adhered to by the parties.

Furthermore, the Loan Document may contain provisions about amendments, waivers, and consents that do not affect the rights or duties of the involved parties. It also includes information on how the Administrative Agent may apply amounts owed under the Loan Documents. Overall, Loan Documents are vital for outlining the specifics of the financial transaction, ensuring all parties understand their rights and obligations in relation to the loans.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a575e820a47b3c2dbd1089d67ed6dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77861f28d368fffce8cb139bd90225db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6cc6030818dd3429d755aaf140adc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d277b1d67ae447d64c60885603bfc58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ea2c276659bea1c507ce8061fac280&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626e172089dfc80733dbdc3d5a655994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcfdf8a71bd320a62004e0e384e11c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d5fd0355f8457b9f5135ee635ccc332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e1f22084ac500ab1a051f7b381aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3501bf74ffa65326e0d3555b82f8a65d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041fd1af71b876447afbbb6e3c656bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505094570d348d1eb98341b07550afb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a3e836c8b1039ab574b4d21c75c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af268fffead491c2994a023017c7b638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30985c7e8f8dee391f2bd509a43ea515&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4792b5b0b77bf53c196055d4d402e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51e0b942fc38bb2172bde4cb6d8e8480&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0d8174003f4772facdd639b135093a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4624e829973bed7d3dbe1f2bc639fd07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49d5badee5a4510f96230df4661d245d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca785d11c173b114c75a86d24a9c1982&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ad4aee590c35f13996d66a7065a0103&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57790ed9c8601659e5a900ae22c9e87f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9164310bb510717cd7cd3ab94e1d97c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23731f788c5c083ebf38a42584c7dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6e59cb00ab074fd4164fff2fb0f72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-904c0cc387dffe2b87a7d3f92f2a414f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e537cc0fdd4eb245e770ae2d38a157f1</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LOANS" refers to the financial amounts lent to the Borrower under the terms established in the Agreement, representing the principal obligation and involving structured financing provided by Lenders. These funds may be evidenced by a promissory note and are subject to repayment as outlined in the Agreement. Any outstanding Loans must be fully paid by the Borrower on the Facility Termination Date. The Loans may reference a Benchmark for interest calculations and include provisions concerning the Defaulting Lender's participation agreements.

In the context of judicial proceedings, these funds borrowed by the Borrower are subject to claims. "LOANS" also entail specific funding obligations that lenders must provide, which may involve multiple parties and are managed by the Administrative Agent. The amounts borrowed, including the monetary values granted under the terms of the credit agreement, may be assigned according to the agreement's stipulations.

Additionally, the financial products discussed may include provisions for Letters of Credit. The amounts are also indicative of structured credit arrangements that Lenders engage in to finance the Borrower. Any foreign currency loans may incur additional costs related to their funding. Ultimately, the term "LOANS" encapsulates the comprehensive framework of borrowed funds, repayment terms, and the structured nature of these financial transactions as set forth by the involved parties under the respective agreements.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-044c8c17addf705b3a705cce6b061dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca04737f45a17e3fb227522494264c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dde35fec0c8bee31e9959cd10aeb752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c568b4b23ac5cd142b7bb3de2e9123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6cc6030818dd3429d755aaf140adc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3e5cabd1adf8bfb109a8c35cc714a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b81ad32680319d4fa9bb79e2517486d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6e6633392fc0a2358006ce0dd843d1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08590c6f860ab659cec13d7e2426aa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443cceb6eea0f4b1688789c95181be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6eb63f465378ef1651901525bcc3ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bfa88e74387e9ded8d6d400ce29b863&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78df53bf404a8c04f30aed8e096f054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fa9414c8f55fa15b04b2759525b64c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9cd184601902e993589a5485493e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c14c7925e4a607de0382cb8d2225da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b2d3addc3724118fcaa9cbe2d864f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52bf93d3e20b62a0cd832df66353f563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2b28c1dc4239fb1b4dc694b26a9338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6e59cb00ab074fd4164fff2fb0f72e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETTER OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LETTER OF CREDIT"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Letter of Credit is a financial instrument issued by a bank, specifically referred to as the Issuing Lender, that guarantees payment to a seller on behalf of a buyer under specified conditions. This guarantees payment, contingent upon the Borrower reimbursing the Lender for any amounts drawn against the Letter of Credit. It serves as a crucial document in financial transactions, particularly in trade, providing assurance to sellers that they will receive payment once the contract terms have been fulfilled.

The issuance of a Letter of Credit may involve various conditions and is typically defined in a credit agreement. These conditions can include the necessity for the Borrower to notify the Administrative Agent of the issuance and potential denominational requirements in different currencies. Furthermore, the availability of the amount that can be drawn under the Letter of Credit is determined according to specific sections outlined in the agreement.

The Letter of Credit represents a guarantee that protects all parties involved, ensuring that payments related to financial commitments are handled correctly. It also plays a vital role in transactions involving revolved loans, foreign currency dealings, and general payment assurances linked with the Borrower's obligations. In the context of issuance, adherence to defined procedures and requirements is emphasized, ensuring that no defaults are waived or overlooked.

Overall, a Letter of Credit is an essential financial document that provides security and assurance in transactions, underscoring its importance in maintaining trust and financial integrity between parties.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a8f315e0d4cc8cd2accfbbe5da06a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ca04737f45a17e3fb227522494264c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7da74967a1a961b1ef138e5868347ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d610724a0ad4c9bf19e1e6f7531d7eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a575e820a47b3c2dbd1089d67ed6dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf07809d1746fad0fc15e800a6e13c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45eacffe710b8a1539c2b0e28ec9c0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91e39b4cb51361795b6a0cd59c0305c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16bc6fb03d3fef88e01a6cce943dfcd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626e172089dfc80733dbdc3d5a655994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94c0222f445089aa6e963934b40deca9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3a44537e6b80de7561b3cfa10fb6a36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50ff3410f6697f7d5609929e33fcaa0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041fd1af71b876447afbbb6e3c656bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1a72299a7c8c944b15ac55292688d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505094570d348d1eb98341b07550afb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3233fa8d7d4c0809069a1ba9245215cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c87b9e7043c61cd132d4af9cb79a608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdb56df8c98cd2c1ef5d8cac7dcfbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6650c2933728727b65a678ab18928dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f81c89a4f0646075ebbb8d120c81f1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b5bfafb78d3fba9840d96ce7e8fc410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c42000811c18c4fe1fb14e6839c213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f248cd4e812b91a37d2ecd4ea05ab17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24b299af046284d0d960e7277a78caa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7c6cce4fccfd6907fab04622874d2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eafbdd125e44e090d5ed4a2ad20dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bfb84ae77fdaa5e8c3a97e04c2e26f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23731f788c5c083ebf38a42584c7dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23cc38126f5fc772e7c16a84edaa089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a52ff11a1589fe75d0346ef535d42ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cbe80e57800f5428ab88cd36b4f48ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78a94bb2c8dc099ee3742dd06619dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc596f8efd3d960e41a0c7ead13fb1fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99d40b4e9dc14bb67b22b82308d7b947</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "DEFAULT" refers to a condition wherein the Borrower fails to meet the obligations set forth in the loan agreement or the Loan Documents. This state signifies a failure to comply with the contractual terms, leading to significant repercussions for both the Borrower and the lenders. Specifically, it indicates that the Borrower has not satisfied their legal obligations as delineated in the agreement, which can affect the rights of lenders and may trigger potential legal actions.

DEFAULT encompasses various scenarios, including instances where the Borrower’s failure impacts the process for appointing a new Administrative Agent and potentially allows for the acceleration of obligations under the agreement. The occurrence of DEFAULT may also permit the Administrative Agent to request inspections of the Borrower’s financial records under certain conditions. Furthermore, it is defined by specific events outlined in Article 7 of the agreement that breach the terms, ultimately affecting the borrower-lender dynamic.

In situations of DEFAULT, any delay or omission by the lenders or Issuing Lenders to exercise their rights under the Loan Documents does not waive their authority to address the DEFAULT or signify acquiescence. Additionally, it is mentioned that, during the period of DEFAULT, it is essential to note that no DEFAULT or Unmatured DEFAULT should be occurring for certain clauses in the agreement to apply. Overall, DEFAULT represents a critical and serious matter in financial agreements, with the potential for substantial financial and legal consequences.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d610724a0ad4c9bf19e1e6f7531d7eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a575e820a47b3c2dbd1089d67ed6dfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf07809d1746fad0fc15e800a6e13c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e50dc3791859bd42e6b79be8ac39d58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a3e836c8b1039ab574b4d21c75c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af268fffead491c2994a023017c7b638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d1e82013d8397017bf069a08e734a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fa9414c8f55fa15b04b2759525b64c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5cae935d5ac1c45cef47e54948aebca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b5bfafb78d3fba9840d96ce7e8fc410&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7ba5dd3dff3a1a68f89de13b8aa21f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c42000811c18c4fe1fb14e6839c213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbd5056a9b1d822dcccb189f309820c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9cd184601902e993589a5485493e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a5395386d972c6903e35205b0eb8cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7fe64f66c3bae5bd7a455b76b08b5bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f0b98aec52fb64b5625c54126b83ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7c6cce4fccfd6907fab04622874d2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c120a778327f296345bae50f8d1508f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c546287864ea4d788574dbe3580df8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8faad6dc190779488071e1a1e21383a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7db23745e08dce95f931014f491b519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da627f496ed5b278745386e332bef7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3679e0426d9ba539d7a46289e2bab63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23cc38126f5fc772e7c16a84edaa089</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
