<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Administrative Agent," specifically identified as Citibank, N.A., plays a crucial role in managing the administrative functions associated with loan agreements and credit products. Acting on behalf of the lenders, the Administrative Agent handles a variety of responsibilities that include ensuring compliance with the terms outlined in the credit agreement, managing relationships between borrowers and lenders, and overseeing the administration of loans and the associated documentation.

As part of its duties, the Administrative Agent is authorized to make decisions on behalf of the lenders regarding waivers, amendments, and compliance with regulatory obligations. The entity also provides quotations and administers the Eurocurrency Base Rate, manages communications related to the loan, including the processing of notices and requests from borrowers, and maintains essential documents such as the Participant Register.

The Administrative Agent is responsible for managing the issuance of Letters of Credit, overseeing financial transactions, ensuring that contractual obligations are met, and managing payments and reallocations among lenders. They also play a key role in implementing changes related to Benchmark Replacement, managing tax withholding obligations, and facilitating communications regarding financial statements related to the borrower.

Additionally, the Administrative Agent is tasked with collecting, processing, and distributing payments based on the borrower's notifications and must keep accurate records of all transactions and communications. This entity conducts its operations under the obligations outlined in the Loan Documents, may appoint sub-agents, and possesses rights to file claims in judicial proceedings concerning the borrower.

It is imperative for the Administrative Agent to ensure all actions taken align with the loan agreements, and significant decisions impacting the Agent's responsibilities must be documented in writing. The Administrative Agent operates as a non-fiduciary entity for the borrower, solely focused on the interests of the lenders.</data>
