<node id="&quot;FOREIGN CURRENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CURRENCY"</data>
  <data key="d1">Foreign Currency refers to any currency other than the Borrower's domestic currency, specifically used in relation to international transactions, loans, and Letters of Credit. It encompasses currencies that may be involved in various financial agreements, including repayments and reimbursements under loan agreements. Foreign Currency can be denominated in a variety of forms, impacting the reimbursement process for Letters of Credit, which may be executed in a currency other than the primary currency used in the transaction. 

In the context of loans and credit facilities, Foreign Currency signifies currencies acknowledged for Eurocurrency loans and letters of credit, requiring requisite approvals. This includes currencies used in international transactions and their relevance for credit transactions, disbursements, and obligations under the Agreement. The equivalent amount in Foreign Currency is determined by the Administrative Agent, particularly concerning the conversion during Advances; however, it cannot be converted into an Alternate Base Rate Advance.

The term also includes any currency that is not the national currency unit of the entity making the loan, which is critical when evaluating the impact of exchange rates. Furthermore, Foreign Currency plays a significant role in calculating obligations tied to syndicated credit facilities, loans, and associated costs. Therefore, it is essential for understanding various aspects of international finance, including the authority of lenders to engage with Foreign Currency in the London interbank market and the types of currencies involved in such agreements. 

Additionally, the document highlights the need for specific timing for payments made in Foreign Currency and underscores the regulations pertaining to alternative forms of currency for transactions, specifically excluding Canadian Dollars and Euros when relevant.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0a8f315e0d4cc8cd2accfbbe5da06a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d610724a0ad4c9bf19e1e6f7531d7eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec8822f0ae2be723af299c5930b2ed8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d35133a09e796f51c620fe44c317a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90c568b4b23ac5cd142b7bb3de2e9123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041fd1af71b876447afbbb6e3c656bab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-505094570d348d1eb98341b07550afb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c87b9e7043c61cd132d4af9cb79a608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-660ba35b7b2352a6dcf5d1814a86b611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-436dbc8e8c3aea78e296e758404cb6e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f248cd4e812b91a37d2ecd4ea05ab17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb0e9645dbfb8d0a148e453d64143d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d2f0619713166fc84a2c2b0e0230d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5688b6fd8f243ed8c9414896fb34a20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d92f3ae85f5d9dc7cd636aa2549b31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eafbdd125e44e090d5ed4a2ad20dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c088153227b34dfaa95e623edf217ee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da627f496ed5b278745386e332bef7e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f007ed84b09aaafd346209ff90f4b1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f1be3cca81841828b69a682f741856e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a52ff11a1589fe75d0346ef535d42ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78a94bb2c8dc099ee3742dd06619dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc596f8efd3d960e41a0c7ead13fb1fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffe12461084bb91bf3fa92e79fc2890e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da412b37f50503895e084a2932cc427</data>
