<node id="&quot;LENDERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The term "Lenders" refers to a group of financial institutions or entities that provide loans to the Borrower under the terms outlined in the relevant credit agreement. These lenders engage in various lending arrangements that may involve issuing Letters of Credit and maintaining financing obligations, which include both Defaulting Lenders and Issuing Lenders. Lenders are responsible for managing payments, making independent credit analyses, and enforcing their rights under the Loan Documents. They also play a crucial role in the decision-making processes related to the agreement, including approving amendments and addressing any defaults.

The Lenders are entitled to receive payments and have claims in judicial proceedings, and they must be informed of any defaults or potential defaults by the Borrower. They are involved in the Benchmark Replacement process, ensuring that they can raise objections within defined parameters. Importantly, Lenders rely on notices purportedly issued by or on behalf of the Borrower, maintaining oversight over the Guaranteed Obligations outlined by the Guarantors.

In partnership with the Administrative Agent, the Lenders are willing to provide revolving credit facilities, adhering to the specific terms set forth in the Loan Documents. They are required to honor requests for credit extensions under certain conditions and are involved in the processes governing jurisdiction, communication, and the consistency of the Borrower’s disclosures. Overall, Lenders are fundamental to the borrowing process, ensuring that all arrangements and obligations are thoroughly defined and upheld.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f7da74967a1a961b1ef138e5868347ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99e694a36ce9e20cd42f9c5918c7a197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1183a800fd6a9854db176c7afeee466f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6cc6030818dd3429d755aaf140adc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ecd873e7a9d5e2ffb5d6892446a1df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edf07809d1746fad0fc15e800a6e13c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebd046b77e404961bb2e85f280bf3765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d88c08aa03f546119db2aa5503fb5d3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88b24f224a12be42ba1f1dbc4b72037c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-175c18fb247e3700a956581f912d57df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3e7677f7f7b78ac8baeaf00df9e5e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3501bf74ffa65326e0d3555b82f8a65d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ca92fb46e43aac35741ad94be06baf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb6e2d4916072445b0d7943e6df0abe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c87b9e7043c61cd132d4af9cb79a608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b3c1b09c7a3b24aa925d3f14133dc8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f443cceb6eea0f4b1688789c95181be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-509c304656080c8e86ce3cd455d89065&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a3e836c8b1039ab574b4d21c75c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb44d7769bde7d6f8440869a5a341430&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-367efea91f14c308908cbf46f7b778de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4ac05f6ad1913c40d66d2f014a76efa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-455f5d24af85e0e01ce99360a0fe0f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01fa9414c8f55fa15b04b2759525b64c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b237e569bb47a68fc1dfc5a53add55c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c42000811c18c4fe1fb14e6839c213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4438bf9135054e1ff77226fc332e8268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbd5056a9b1d822dcccb189f309820c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2784e996404efd1f12a712b7977889c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24419696c56548b55b76e26989b6a45a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5a5395386d972c6903e35205b0eb8cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6325bfa6d1cd9b9d3bc87034e1d3d3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b0d8174003f4772facdd639b135093a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d984b41314faeae1eec3c3d4885dafca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c546287864ea4d788574dbe3580df8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87fd223bdbce8cbc5531c412e0930ce1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-039451d90b356c9b728719b3f47939fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63f7f879e70c1c09e23862d87cf18c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2b28c1dc4239fb1b4dc694b26a9338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a78ac18a08e4ac60633a82d5e95b9af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50d92f3ae85f5d9dc7cd636aa2549b31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c69c40f76d1bb8ba3d996a93ada3d2c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b4182c08d76c1d482af7a301493f62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a73a441bb280da7c7eac26f41db97d87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7fec4fdd82d22a739ed83a9be76e9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23731f788c5c083ebf38a42584c7dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63d40e5eaf64a1cf442eb0d95460cb74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23cc38126f5fc772e7c16a84edaa089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-904c0cc387dffe2b87a7d3f92f2a414f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee99ae045b011273b805e2d9acdc4dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da412b37f50503895e084a2932cc427</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-0a132332ec994ff64af411572927a941</data>
  <data key="d4">citibank-gxo</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULTING LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">A Defaulting Lender is defined as a lender that has failed to meet its obligations under the terms of the loan agreement, significantly impacting the rights of other parties involved, such as the Administrative Agent and the Borrower. This failure can lead to complications in the repayment and collateral arrangements, affecting the distribution of payments not only to the Lenders but also to the Issuing Lenders. A Defaulting Lender is typically determined by the Administrative Agent based on specific clauses outlined in the agreement and is identified through a written notice.

In this context, a Defaulting Lender may neglect their financial obligations, including missed funding commitments or failure to comply with stipulated fees, resulting in various operational difficulties within the loan transaction. The consequences extend to restrictions on the Defaulting Lender's rights, such as the inability to approve or disapprove amendments or waivers related to the agreement, and their status is further complicated by the potential reallocation of commitments among Non-Defaulting Lenders.

Moreover, the presence of a Defaulting Lender affects the application of cash collateral, which is crucial for ensuring that creditors can meet their claims. In situations where a lender is unable to fulfill its obligations or declares intentions to default, all assignments to the Defaulting Lender will be viewed similarly until compliance is achieved. Lastly, any request for information regarding the status of Defaulting Lenders, including the revocation of such designation, can be directed to the Administrative Agent, underscoring the importance of monitoring a Defaulting Lender's compliance with the credit agreement.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9ed9d7d04f3944a560b6db90e5050458&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c340d96c262ce6b46bd104eff6e1e898&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d610724a0ad4c9bf19e1e6f7531d7eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc38152b0f228851eb2001881889cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dde35fec0c8bee31e9959cd10aeb752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07d22735da3f44da96c1e4f1bea670b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3e5cabd1adf8bfb109a8c35cc714a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16bc6fb03d3fef88e01a6cce943dfcd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-626e172089dfc80733dbdc3d5a655994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5f19a0770314c9062282c6df3f08fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e08590c6f860ab659cec13d7e2426aa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a3e836c8b1039ab574b4d21c75c56d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-367efea91f14c308908cbf46f7b778de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83c42000811c18c4fe1fb14e6839c213&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbd5056a9b1d822dcccb189f309820c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f8540eaf8f40e45748d1788b0ef6de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9cd184601902e993589a5485493e18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb0e9645dbfb8d0a148e453d64143d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03b2d3addc3724118fcaa9cbe2d864f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bfb84ae77fdaa5e8c3a97e04c2e26f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e55ec0667ebf49101d269a842009d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e631a64c88c6919f8b9a9bcae9c00286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13482f9d41736bece8f6cc18418a9fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef03c2a3bc83b467c592d30c98456018</data>
