<node id="&quot;PERSON&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"OBLIGOR"</data>
  <data key="d1">A "Person" refers to any legal individual or entity that can enter into contracts, specifically encompassing various roles and obligations within the context of agreements, particularly in relation to financial transactions, loan documents, and currency exchange. This term is inclusive of any individual or entity involved in contractual obligations under the agreement, such as Borrowers, Lenders, and other parties, and extends to those defined as having claims or rights under these agreements.

In this context, a Person may be entitled to receive loans, have obligations pertaining to lease agreements, and may also include individuals or entities that have dependency on or rights under the credit agreements affecting obligations and rights, extending to any parties involved with the Borrower or related entities. Moreover, it can refer to legal definitions including any organization or individual with ownership stakes or governance structure relevant to the Borrower, as well as those engaged in the acquisition of assets or participating in transactions as related to the Borrower's Indebtedness.

The term also addresses specific roles, such as the Administrative Agent or individuals acting on behalf of Lenders, indicating their accountability under the terms of the agreement. Understanding the breadth of the term "Person" is essential, as it applies to anyone legally bound by obligations outlined in the agreements, including but not limited to financial commitments, asset ownership, and various conditions tied to the arrangement, such as the eligibility for assignments or the potential for restructuring or merging with the Borrower.

In summary, "Person" encapsulates a broad spectrum of individuals and entities involved in legal, financial, and contractual frameworks, highlighting their varied and intricate relationships and obligations as dictated by the Agreement.</data>
